<title>FRANCE: Renault rises ahead of key general meeting.</title>
<headline>Renault rises ahead of key general meeting.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Renault were up strongly ahead of a key general meeting on Tuesday at which the closure of a plant in Vilvoorde, Belgium, is set to be discussed.</p>
<p>The new French government will state this week what is its position on the closure plan. The state has a minority stake in Renault.</p>
<p>Prime Minister Lionel Jospin met his Belgian counterpart Jean-Luc Dehaene on Saturday but gave no public hints whether the state would push the carmaker into changing its decision.</p>
<p>At 0854 GMT, Renault was up 2.63 percent at 140.5 francs.</p>
</text>
